#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129253 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129078 :question/id #uuid "53aa15a0-8633-51b8-8731-9099eec94940" :question/math-academy-id "e-9941" :question/problem "![](images/26/2683c694582a7c2dbe1c95cce6af22ef941a1e77b54721151a935e81ec2b3b1a.png)\n\nA part of the graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is given above. Which of the following statements is true?\n\n- $x=-4$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity\n\n- $x=-4$ is a multiple root of even multiplicity\n\n- $x=-4$ is a simple root" :question/worked-solution "| Multiplicity | Sketch | Sketch |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ \n\n (Simple Root) | ![](images/5a/5a0221f93c65a1eeb4503604a558a6da81c4c7af81c2c52cc35ecf3d189fe99f.png) | ![](images/d5/d556b4edf39181eebb7ec87c344d6f657a6875ecd2745405eaf5351ccaff6f96.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Even | ![](images/9d/9d14c2588da2ee9c9f5bbc32a70791146bed609ea0d6d5912aeaa2edab02e2d7.png) | ![](images/28/28ad9248a9a509e3a44937d0438fb2366f550a22360d01b9b6a29bcac41357e8.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Odd | ![](images/3a/3ae81378cb3c918dd5b7730519eb5a91e949f88eef9f03f4910f4ab8fb3cd5a9.png) | ![](images/95/9506a7ce4031f1f6244c0110c3235f66ea5652bb53548a032732869cf21f5997.png) |\n\nIt's possible to determine information regarding the multiplicities of the roots of a polynomial from its graph.\n\n- If the graph intersects the $x$-axis but is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *simple* root $x=a.$\n\n- If the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *multiple* root $x=a.$ Furthermore:\n\n- If the graph touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *even*.\n\n- If the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *odd*.\n\nIn our case, the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=-4.$ So, $x=-4$ is a *multiple* root. \n\nFurthermore, the graph touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=-4.$ So, $x=-4$ has *even* multiplicity.\n\nTherefore, $x=-4$ is a multiple root of even multiplicity."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d48e2a0-1a76-5eec-a98c-4a7eb16f70cb" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048669 :topic/math-academy-id 88 :topic/title "Multiplicities of the Roots of Polynomials"}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518544 :question-generator/id #uuid "1bd70471-b297-5e2b-8148-13cb101610d5" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186129253.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129495 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a5e1ad2-1530-5ea9-afd0-b8821e67489f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 3$ is a simple root" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126471} {:answer/id #uuid "b940577f-2c1c-5880-a99b-02e525839d37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 3$ is a multiple root of even multiplicity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126472} {:answer/id #uuid "0ceac3b7-c7d5-5c42-8a20-1f2b0f06b7cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 3$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126473} {:answer/id #uuid "4b63a343-8aae-5d66-9e41-c67c5eb894fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 3$ is not a root of $p(x)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126474} {:answer/id #uuid "7711f0f7-1ff6-56fa-bee0-58f1ffec3040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 3$ is a simple root of even multiplicity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126475}] :answer-field/id #uuid "99c6317b-2913-5842-8456-613c95eb39c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126470}] :question/id #uuid "7d255093-6f1a-5d48-a501-a1e3241dcefa" :question/math-academy-id "q-140411" :question/problem "![](images/76/7622b937c07cb6cac17925901290823d375b92bb08980cec86938f4795a3fc14.png)\n\nA part of the graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is given above. Which of the follow